  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-find-plugin [](https://awesome-dsh-plugin.com)",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n**A plugin that finds plugins** — think [`/find-skills`](https://skills.sh) from skills.sh, for DSH.\n\nTell your agent what you want (\"notify me on WeChat when a task finishes\"),\nand it searches the DSH plugin ecosystem on GitHub for you — top results by\nstars, each with a one-line description and an install command.\n\n<img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/awesome-dsh-plugin/dsh-find-plugin/main/assets/demo-en.png\" alt=\"find_dsh_plugin in action\" width=\"640\">"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "from npm (prebuilt, recommended)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-find-plugin"
    },
    {
      "section": "or from GitHub",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add github:awesome-dsh-plugin/dsh-find-plugin\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Restart `dsh web` after installing, then just talk to the agent — it calls\n`find_dsh_plugin` on its own whenever plugin discovery helps:\n\n- \"What terminal TUI plugins are there?\"\n- \"I want to get a WeChat notification when a task finishes — any plugin for that?\"\n- \"Find me something for reviewing git diffs inside DSH.\"\n\nEach result comes back with stars, a description, the repo link, and a\nready-to-run `dsh plugin add` command — ask the agent to install one and\nit can run the command for you."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "- Live GitHub repository search scoped to the official `dsh-plugin` topic,\n  re-ranked by stars (5-minute per-query cache).\n- When a result is also listed on\n  [awesome-dsh-plugin](https://awesome-dsh-plugin.com), its hand-written\n  bilingual description from `plugins.json` replaces the GitHub one (the\n  `lang` parameter picks the language) — ranking is untouched.\n- Every result comes with a ready-to-run `dsh plugin add` command. Plugins\n  are third-party code — review the source and pin a commit."
    },
